    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0324" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg252"/>

                <head>No. 25.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. West
                        to Earl Granville.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 20, 1882</date>.
                        (Received March 4.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    to your lordship copy of a dispatch which I have received from Her Majesty’s
                    consul at Baltimore, inclosing copies of an extract from the Baltimore American,
                    containing a notice of the case of Denis H. O’Connor, now imprisoned in Ireland,
                    and who is one of those mentioned in the resolutions introduced in the House of
                    Representatives, on the subject of which I had the honor to address your
                    lordship in my dispatch of the 15th instant.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d150-a1.xml" xpointer="d150-a1"/>
